  "$readme": "AAP 2022 Hyperbilirubinemia Management Guidelines — phototherapy and exchange transfusion thresholds. Source: Kemper AR, et al. Clinical Practice Guideline Revision: Management of Hyperbilirubinemia in the Newborn Infant 35 or More Weeks of Gestation. Pediatrics 2022;150(3):e2022058859. License: AAP CC-BY-NC. Threshold values in mg/dL TSB. Risk strata: low (≥38 wk, no neurotoxicity risk factors), medium (38+ wk with risk factors OR 35–37+6 wk no risk), high (35–37+6 wk with risk factors). Hyperbilirubinemia neurotoxicity risk factors per AAP 2022: gestational age <38 weeks (lower GA = higher risk), albumin <3.0 g/dL, isoimmune hemolytic disease (positive DAT), G6PD deficiency, sepsis, significant clinical instability in previous 24 h. Hour-of-life anchors are interpolated linearly at runtime.",
